Plimail
https://github.com/laupernoe/plimail

Plimail is a fork of MailFlow by Matt (https://github.com/maathimself/mailflow),
licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0. The full licence text is in
LICENSE. Copyright in the original code remains with its authors.

This is a modified version of MailFlow. Modifications since 2026-11-11 (the date of the
fork) include:

  - Renamed the product to Plimail: interface text in every locale, page titles, PWA
    manifest, backend-sent product name (X-Mailer, User-Agent, emails), desktop and
    Android shells.
  - New monochrome logo, favicon, PWA, desktop and Android icons.
  - Calendars: CalDAV accounts and calendars, calendar settings, upcoming pane.
  - Removed the upstream project's sponsorship links, business-licence notice,
    commercial licence, contributor licence agreement, funding and code-owner files,
    and pointed the update check, package metadata and CI image names at the fork.
  - Added a Source code link (AGPL-3.0 section 13) to Settings, About.
  - Removed the plugin platform and the GTD plugin, the Todoist and CardDAV
    contact-sync integrations, the built-in antispam filter and the mailbox cleanup tool.
  - Simplified the stack to one image: the backend serves the built frontend itself over
    HTTP, replacing the nginx frontend image, its TLS handling and the bundled Caddy.
  - Removed the Electron desktop app, the Capacitor Android app and their release workflow.

Internal identifiers that installed copies depend on (MAILFLOW_* environment variables,
database and role names, cookie and storage keys, data-mailflow-* attributes, Docker
volume names) keep their original names.

The upstream project's commercial licence offer does not apply to Plimail, which is
distributed under the AGPL-3.0 only.
